---
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import Panel from "~/components/illustration-kit/Panel.astro"

// All six three-flip sequences with at least one flip following H.
// TTH and TTT have no such flip, so their rate is undefined.
const rows = ["HHH", "HHT", "HTH", "HTT", "THH", "THT"].map((sequence) => {
  const flips = sequence.split("").map((value, index) => ({
    value,
    counted: index > 0 && sequence[index - 1] === "H",
    tone: value === "H" ? "bg-series-gold text-ink" : "bg-series-blue text-paper",
  }))
  const following = flips.filter((flip) => flip.counted)
  return {
    sequence,
    flips,
    heads: following.filter((flip) => flip.value === "H").length,
    total: following.length,
  }
})
const countedFlips = rows.flatMap((row) => row.flips.filter((flip) => flip.counted))
---

<IllustrationFigure name="hot-hand" lead="The same flips, counted two different ways">
  <p class="text-base leading-normal">
    Flip a fair coin three times. H means heads (like a hit in basketball); T means tails (a
    miss). Count a flip only if the preceding flip was H. Red outlines show which flips count.
  </p>
  <div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] gap-3 border-b-2 border-ink pb-2 font-bold">
      <span>Three flips, in order</span>
      <span>Heads / counted</span>
    </div>
    {rows.map((row) => (
      <div class="grid grid-cols-[1fr_auto] items-center gap-3 border-b border-ink/20 py-2">
        <div class="flex min-w-0 gap-1.5" aria-label={`Sequence ${row.sequence}`}>
          {row.flips.map((flip) => (
            <span
              class:list={[
                "flex size-10 items-center justify-center border-2 font-mono font-bold",
                flip.counted ? ["border-series-red", flip.tone] : "border-ink/30 text-ink/60",
              ]}
            >
              {flip.value}
            </span>
          ))}
        </div>
        <span class="min-w-14 text-right font-mono text-base font-bold">
          {row.heads}/{row.total}
        </span>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="text-sm leading-normal">
    TTH and TTT are left out: neither has a flip after H, so there is no rate to average.
  </p>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <Panel title="Count each marked flip">
      <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-normal">Put all eight marked flips together.</p>
      <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5" aria-hidden="true">
        {countedFlips.map((flip) => (
          <span
            class:list={[
              "flex size-9 items-center justify-center border-2 border-series-red font-bold",
              flip.tone,
            ]}
          >
            {flip.value}
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base">Four of the eight are H.</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-2xl font-bold">4/8 = 50%</p>
    </Panel>
    <Panel title="Count each sequence once">
      <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-normal">Give each row's rate equal weight.</p>
      <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-3 gap-1.5">
        {rows.map((row) => (
          <span class="flex items-center justify-center border border-ink p-1 font-mono font-bold">
            {row.heads}/{row.total}
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base">Average the six rates.</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-2xl font-bold">5/12 ≈ 42%</p>
    </Panel>
  </div>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    HHH contributes two heads after heads (2/2); HTH contributes a tail after a head (0/1).
    Pooling counts HHH twice but HTH once, while averaging the sequence rates gives both equal
    weight. That weighting difference helps explain the 42% result, even though the coin is
    fair. The pooled 50% is only a comparison for this coin example, not a correction to the
    basketball study.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
